# Backend conventions

Fat services / thin views. `Decimal` for money, UTC for all datetimes, type hints
throughout (`mypy` in CI), `ruff` for lint+format. Models in
`apps/<name>/models.py`, business logic in a service layer, tests alongside.

## Tenancy and RLS

- Tenant-owned models inherit `apps.core.models.BaseModel` and are queried only
  through the default `objects` manager. `Model.all_objects` is for deliberate,
  explicit cross-client access.
- Every concrete `BaseModel` subclass's migration must also apply
  `apps.core.migration_operations.EnableRowLevelSecurity(model_name)`. RLS is a
  second, DB-level layer; `all_objects` bypasses only the ORM filter, not it.
- Code touching `BaseModel` rows outside an HTTP request (management command,
  Celery task) must call `apps.core.rls.set_rls_session_vars(client_id,
  is_platform_staff)` inside an open transaction first, or every query is
  silently empty and every write is rejected. For system code with no
  authenticated platform-staff request, use `apps.core.rls.platform_staff_bypass()`.
- Connect to Postgres as `integra_app`, never `integra` (bootstrap superuser
  bypasses RLS unconditionally).

## Two evaluation-time traps with `TenantScopedManager`

Both evaluate once at import time, before any request has set a tenancy context,
and freeze to an empty queryset forever.

```python
# BAD — class attribute, evaluated at import
class BusinessListView(ListAPIView):
    queryset = Business.objects.all()

# GOOD — method, evaluated per request
class BusinessListView(ListAPIView):
    def get_queryset(self):
        return Business.objects.all()
```

```python
# BAD — declared serializer fields are collected at class-body execution
class RoleSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):
    role = serializers.PrimaryKeyRelatedField(queryset=Role.objects.all())

# GOOD — resolve the FK inside validate_<field>()
class RoleSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):
    def validate_role(self, value):
        return Role.objects.get(pk=value)
```

`.all_objects` is contextvar-free and safe as a class attribute.

## Permissions

Gate endpoints with `apps.core.permissions.HasPermission(codename)` against
DB-backed RBAC, not coarse role checks.

## Commands

`uv run pytest`, `uv run ruff check .`, `uv run mypy .`. Regenerate the OpenAPI
spec with `uv run python manage.py spectacular --file openapi.yaml --validate`
whenever the API surface changes; `./scripts/check_openapi_drift.sh` fails on a
stale spec. If a full `pytest` run fails many unrelated tests in a
permission/tenancy-shaped way, run `pytest --create-db` once before chasing it.
